# 12. Required test scenarios

Add or update automated tests where the current project testing architecture supports them.

At minimum verify:

### Extraction

```text
✓ Square-bracket substring is extracted correctly
✓ Existing extraction behavior remains intact
✓ Auto-map identifies the correct source field
```

### Auto-fill

```text
✓ Extracted value populates a normal text field
✓ Extracted value populates a modified/transformed field
✓ Extracted value populates a Date Only field
✓ Extracted value populates a Time Only field
```

### Date

Verify that the resulting value is in the exact format required by the Date Only control.

For example, if using an HTML date input:

```text
YYYY-MM-DD
```

### Time

Verify that the resulting value is in the exact format required by the Time Only control.

For example:

```text
HH:mm
```

Use the format actually required by the current implementation rather than assuming it.

### Visibility

```text
✓ Always visible + auto-filled → visible
✓ Not always visible + auto-filled → remains governed by visibility rules
✓ Auto-fill does not force visibility
✓ Hidden field does not become permanently visible merely because it has a value
✓ Existing visibility behavior continues working for non-auto-filled fields
```

### Persistence

```text
✓ Save template
✓ Reload template
✓ Extractable configuration remains intact
✓ Auto-map remains intact
✓ Control type remains intact
✓ Visibility setting remains intact
```

### UI

```text
✓ "Auto-maps: ..." is not shown to ordinary agents
✓ "Auto-fill: ..." is not shown to ordinary agents
✓ Admin configuration information remains available where appropriate
```

