# 14. Implementation principles

### Do:

- Reuse existing extraction architecture.
- Reuse existing auto-map configuration.
- Reuse existing visibility logic where possible.
- Preserve backwards compatibility with existing templates.
- Keep source and target fields clearly separated.
- Normalize values according to the target control type.
- Keep configuration metadata separate from runtime presentation.
- Add regression tests.

### Do not:

- Rewrite the entire extractable-field system.
- Introduce a second extraction mechanism.
- Hardcode individual template names.
- Hardcode specific field names.
- Make auto-fill automatically imply visibility.
- Remove functionality simply because it is difficult to fix.
- Fix the Admin preview while leaving runtime broken.
- Hide errors by silently discarding incompatible values.

---

# 15. Final acceptance criteria

The feature should be considered fixed only when this complete workflow works:

```text
Admin creates/edits template
        ↓
Marks part of a field using [square brackets]
        ↓
Maps extracted value to a target field
        ↓
Configures target control type
        ↓
Configures visibility
        ↓
Saves template
        ↓
Agent opens template
        ↓
Extraction occurs
        ↓
Correct substring is obtained
        ↓
Auto-map executes
        ↓
Correct transformation occurs
        ↓
Target field receives value
        ↓
Target control displays value correctly
        ↓
Visibility rules remain respected
```

And the agent-facing interface should contain **no unnecessary `Auto-maps:` or `Auto-fill:` labels**.

